from helpers import *
# Games Bandai Namco developed or published (the wiki's publisher or developer field), not covered by an earlier pack.
# P = passthrough, for games the wiki or Steam say have controller support and that came out after XInput (Dec 2005).
# PS = passthrough plus a gyro profile, for shooters (see GYRO_PT_NOTE in engine.py).
# G = generated pointer pack (or arrow keys), for games with no controller support.
# ctl= ticks the pad kinds the game supports itself: dualshock when the wiki says PlayStation controllers are supported, dualsense when Steam
# also lists DualSense, switch_pro when the wiki says Nintendo controllers are supported. A Steam badge alone does not count.
# Left out: games with no Steam id (Digimon online games, the DOS and Windows 3.x ports, Pac-Man World 3 and Rally, Namco Museum 50th, the
# Mac-only and mobile ports), games whose Steam page is gone (Battleline: Steel Warfare, God Eater: Resurrection, Lumines, Project COLD Case
# Mirage, Rise of Incarnates, SD Shin Kamen Rider Rumble, Star Trek, Super Robot Wars V and X, Test Drive Unlimited 2, The Idolmaster: Starlit
# Season, Young Justice: Legacy), cancelled or shut-down games (Ridge Racer Driftopia, Duelyst, Gundam Evolution, Blue Protocol), Digimon Masters
# Online (online-only; Steam's only executable is its launcher), Little Nightmares VR (a tracked-controller VR game), Project CARS - Pagani
# Edition (a stub of an uncovered game), and games where Steam credits another publisher and the wiki names Bandai Namco only for a regional
# retail release (The Witcher 2, Lords of the Fallen 2014, Project CARS, Warhammer: Mark of Chaos, The Journeyman Project, Street Racing
# Syndicate, MUD, DeadCore, GoD Factory: Wingmen, Beware Planet Earth, Puzzle Quest: Galactrix).
# Steam ids are each game's base app; demos and DLC are not rules.
